{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Post-close alarm hygiene (2026-09-09 about 06:04-06:13 UTC): a final CloudWatch check caught rebar-docker-buildkit-cache-high back in ALARM after subsequent cache growth (six 91% datapoints). I remediated with the live bounded-retention mechanism, docker builder prune --force --keep-storage 4gb, which reduced Build Cache to 4.291 GB (about 79%). A fresh observability tick published 79% datapoints at 23:08/23:13 PDT, and the alarm returned to OK at 23:09 PDT. This reinforces that the cap/alarm/reclaim path is live and repeatable."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788934763751359001,"uuid":"96225079-dfed-4ea6-bb44-34f14f2bd133"}